{
	"_comment": "Commodity markets. Every port buys and sells every commodity. A commodity's price at a port starts as its base price x its region's multiplier (or the port's own, from sources); it's then evened out with nearby ports (a weighted average over sea distance, the weight falling off over smoothing_nm, as competing traders would) so neighbours price alike and differences grow with distance; then x a gentle local variation (up to local_variation between ports, varying smoothly across the map) x a coastal variation (typically up to coastal_variation either way, from coastal_waves waves across the globe about coastal_wavelength_nm long, different for each commodity, so neighbouring coasts differ a little and short runs can pay) x a slow drift (up to drift, over about drift_period_s) x the market impact of the player's own trades. Region multipliers run from 0.5 (where it's produced) to 2.0 (where it's scarce), a 4x spread. That's what a port pays you for it (the sell price); buying there costs spread more. impact: selling a load lowers the port's sell price by up to impact_max (for a load worth impact_ref_value or more; smaller loads move it less) and buying raises it the same way, recovering with a half-life of impact_half_life_s. base prices are per unit of hold space in each ship line's unit (containers, tons, pallets, head, vehicles; hold: how many units of hold one takes, 1 if not given: a horse takes three head's room), set so similar ships earn alike. xp_ref_price: a commodity's XP per unit per nm is its base price / xp_ref_price x game_config xp_per_container_nm. fuel_per_oil: ships buy their own fuel at the port's oil sell price x this. Base prices were halved (2026-10-08), xp_ref_price and impact_ref_value with them so XP and market impact per load stayed the same; fuel follows the oil price, so it halved too.",
	"local_variation": 0.16,
	"coastal_variation": 0.027,
	"coastal_wavelength_nm": 1600,
	"coastal_waves": 6,
	"smoothing_nm": 1200,
	"spread": 0.05,
	"drift": 0.05,
	"drift_period_s": 1200,
	"impact_max": 0.01,
	"impact_ref_value": 25000000,
	"impact_half_life_s": 40,
	"xp_ref_price": 2000,
	"fuel_per_oil": 0.0028,
